# Session: Slot assignment

## intent: Replace mockfast mutation with a Next.js API route stub, and wire saving/error UI for assignment (pessimistic update)

## What works:

- Assigning an employee calls Next.js api instead of mockfast
- /api/shift-slots/[id] returns "{ok: true, assigned: {slotId, employeeId}}"
- UI locks while saving
- Error path added into Assign modal (modal stays open and shows inline error)
- Local state updates only after success (pessimistic update)

## Compromises:

- Shift-slot updates are stored in local client state only (refresh resets)
- Api response is currently a stub (no validation/persistence; echoes response)
- Error handling is wired, but not being used yet - no real backend

## Out of scope

- Backend persistence / database
- Availability / overlap checks
- Role-based permissions

